course: dictionary
lesson: 5972
title: Max: a word, a name and more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Max is a word with several jobs. Most often it is short for «maximum», the biggest amount possible. «It'll take ten minutes max» means ten minutes at the most, and no longer.
explain: Max is also a name, like the boy in «Max got a Lego set for his birthday.» A capital M at the start of a name is a clue. When you meet max, ask: does the sentence make sense as a name, or as the biggest amount?
explain: Max can be a verb too. To max out means to use up everything you are allowed, so «maxed out the card» means spent right up to the limit. On a cooker or a game, turn it up to max means turn it to the highest setting.
fact: Max is short for maximum, which means the biggest amount possible.
fact: «Ten minutes max» means ten minutes at the most.
fact: «To the max» is slang for completely or as much as possible.
fact: Max is also a boy's name, short for Maximilian or Maxwell.
fact: In maths and computing, max is the largest value in a set of numbers, and min is the smallest.
exercise: Mum says, «Ten minutes max, then bed.» What does max mean here? | Never ever | Exactly twenty minutes | *At the most | At least one hour
exercise: «Max got a Lego set for his birthday.» In this sentence, what is Max? | Something you do with a card | A petrol station | The biggest amount | *A boy's name
exercise: Leo says, «Turn the game up to max!» What does max mean? | Turned off | *Highest setting | Quietest setting | Slowest speed
test: In maths, max means the | Smallest value in a set | Middle number | *Largest value in a set | Number of numbers in a set
test: «He maxed out the card» means he | Gave it to his brother | *Used up all the money allowed on it | Saved all his money | Lost it in the park
exam: Which sentence uses max as a name? | *Max's planner came home to be signed. | He is working at max speed. | Turn the cooker up to max. | Ten minutes max, please.
